# Toolchain version pins — the single source of truth for the gate tooling.
#
# Read by BOTH install paths:
#   - scripts/ci/setup-local-tools.sh               (local)
#   - .github/actions/setup-python-tools/action.yml  (CI)
#
# Why one file: the same four pins used to be written out twice, once per
# install path, and a pin that moved in one copy and not the other made a local
# run and a CI run of the same gate disagree — which reads as a broken gate
# rather than as a version skew. scripts/tests/test_toolchain_pins.py fails if
# a version is written anywhere else.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line, plain shell assignments. No command
# substitution, no expansion of a variable that may be unset — safe to source
# under `set -euo pipefail`.
#
# The three Python packages are pinned to the version PyPI knows (no leading
# "v"). actionlint has no Python distribution: its pin is a GitHub release tag,
# and the asset name is derived from it (the tag without the leading "v"), so
# the release and the file that release ships cannot drift apart.
#
# To move a version, change it here. Nothing else may repeat one.

LYCHEE_BIN_VERSION=0.24.2
YAMLLINT_VERSION=1.38.0
SHELLCHECK_PY_VERSION=0.11.0.1
ACTIONLINT_VERSION=v1.7.7
